@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2832 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [860 x i8] }> <{ [860 x i8] c"# `no_sanitize`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#39699]\0A\0A[#39699]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/39699\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThe `no_sanitize` attribute can be used to selectively disable sanitizer\0Ainstrumentation in an annotated function. This might be useful to: avoid\0Ainstrumentation overhead in a performance critical function, or avoid\0Ainstrumenting code that contains constructs unsupported by given sanitizer.\0A\0AThe precise effect of this annotation depends on particular sanitizer in use.\0AFor example, with `no_sanitize(thread)`, the thread sanitizer will no longer\0Ainstrument non-atomic store / load operations, but it will instrument atomic\0Aoperations to avoid reporting false positives and provide meaning full stack\0Atraces.\0A\0A## Examples\0A\0A``` rust\0A#![feature(no_sanitize)]\0A\0A#[no_sanitize(address)]\0Afn foo() {\0A  // ...\0A}\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
